title: "ClickHouse® vs Elasticsearch: Can ClickHouse® handle search?"
excerpt: "Compare ClickHouse® vs Elasticsearch for analytics and search workloads, including performance, costs, and when to use each database for your specific use case."

### JSON DSL and pipeline tooling in Elasticsearch

Elasticsearch queries use nested JSON that can get complex quickly. Here's a basic aggregation:

```json
{
  "query": {
    "range": {
      "timestamp": {
        "gte": "now-1d"
      }
    }
  },

Tools like Kibana provide visual query builders that generate the JSON for you. However, programmatic queries still require building JSON structures rather than composing SQL strings.

## Performance comparison on ingest, storage, and aggregations

The inverted index overhead means Elasticsearch typically uses [12x to 19x more disk space](https://clickhouse.com/blog/clickhouse_vs_elasticsearch_the_billion_row_matchup) than ClickHouse{% sup %}®{% /sup %} for the same raw data.

[Kafka acts as a buffer](https://www.tinybird.co/blog/enriching-kafka-streams-in-real-time) between systems, with producers writing events once and multiple consumers reading for different purposes.

